{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/589664-seeking-inspiration-what-could-this-abyssal-be-up-to","id":589664,"title":"Seeking Inspiration: What could this abyssal be up to?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-13T17:21:34-07:00","id":589664,"title":"Seeking Inspiration: What could this abyssal be up to?","content":"I recently started a new campaign. Solars in a cyberpunk version of the setting. The characters have met a most charming abyssal girl who killed a whole crowd and raised them as zombies, trying to take hostages. What could she have wanted the hostages for? Maybe to put pressure on the local government (a small island state in the southwest)? Maybe for access to some manse or artifact? I think I need some fresh ideas to flesh out the enemy agenda, including the master the abyssal serves.<br /> Also the realm has taken notice of anathema activities and send a small fleet with an aircraft carrier at its center. They have only limited cooperation from local authorities, but they might well have a circle of dragonblooded, quite a few aircraft and probably a dragon of ground troops, complete with tanks and all that. Any special ideas what they might try to find the anathema (PCs as well as their special &quot;friend&quot;, the abyssal girl)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5584-quaint","name":"Quaint","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T17:35:55-07:00","id":589691,"title":"","content":"Wait.... are the zombies hostages? I'm confused about the wording of your description.<br /> <br /> Assuming you meant that the girl has control of both zombies and hostages, here's some ideas:<br /> <b>1. Rip off Diehard - </b>The girl is claiming allegiance to a Deathlord and demanding the release of some other abyssals who were recently captured by the realm, but this is a smokescreen - she really just wants to steal a huge amount of jade that the island has in storage (the island is a holding area for Realm tribute goods). She'll use the hostage negotiation to fake her death and escape with the money.<br /> <br /> <b>2. </b><b>Distraction - </b>Moving that small Realm fleet out of the way was the real reason for doing this - everything else the abyssal girl does was just stalling. Maybe there's an attack planned on wherever that fleet came from, or there's a secret attack force planning to ambush the fleet (I'm picturing that scene from Pirates of the Carribean where skeletal pirates swarm up over the sides of a ship to board it - that'd be a badass way to steal an aircraft carrier).<br /> <br /> <b>3. Actually, the Solars are the target - </b>The Abyssal is an agent who wants to eliminate the solar party. She expects them to try to save the hostages, and has laid a trap for them. If they escape the trap or she runs out of time, she'll flee and leave them holding the bag (and the blame for the whole crisis) when the Realm fleet shows up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T18:27:22-07:00","id":589741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/589664-seeking-inspiration-what-could-this-abyssal-be-up-to?p=589691#post589691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait.... are the zombies hostages? I'm confused about the wording of your description.<br /> <br /> Assuming you meant that the girl has control of both zombies and hostages, here's some ideas:<br /> <b>1. Rip off Diehard - </b>The girl is claiming allegiance to a Deathlord and demanding the release of some other abyssals who were recently captured by the realm, but this is a smokescreen - she really just wants to steal a huge amount of jade that the island has in storage (the island is a holding area for Realm tribute goods). She'll use the hostage negotiation to fake her death and escape with the money.<br /> <br /> <b>2. </b><b>Distraction - </b>Moving that small Realm fleet out of the way was the real reason for doing this - everything else the abyssal girl does was just stalling. Maybe there's an attack planned on wherever that fleet came from, or there's a secret attack force planning to ambush the fleet (I'm picturing that scene from Pirates of the Carribean where skeletal pirates swarm up over the sides of a ship to board it - that'd be a badass way to steal an aircraft carrier).<br /> <br /> <b>3. Actually, the Solars are the target - </b>The Abyssal is an agent who wants to eliminate the solar party. She expects them to try to save the hostages, and has laid a trap for them. If they escape the trap or she runs out of time, she'll flee and leave them holding the bag (and the blame for the whole crisis) when the Realm fleet shows up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the idea is that the crowd originally were meant to be hostages and things went poorly. Which resulted in zombies. <br /> <br /> Meat shield is always a good one. I mean just because you can take more hits than a mortal doesn't mean you want to and anything that deters people taking shots at you is a good thing in most cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T04:46:00-07:00","id":590145,"title":"","content":"Sorry for my poor english. Actually they were at a large beach cafe and the abyssal killed about half of the people there. They were raised as zombies. Then they tried to take the other half of the people, maybe 70 or 80, hostage. The solar PCs put up a fight however and prevented this. It has been hinted, that the solar only were there because fate had been nudged in that direction and that much worse things would have happened without them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5584-quaint","name":"Quaint","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}